      "body": "@stevenroose Could you confirm the intended validity rule here?\r\n\r\nThe long-form encoding says, “For both inputs and then outputs, expect an additional byte.” I interpreted that as requiring both selector bytes, which would make the currently accepted 2- and 3-byte forms invalid.\r\n\r\nThis PR therefore rejects those truncated forms and updates the generated vectors to explicit 4-byte selectors. As @fametrano pointed out, this is a semantic tightening of the reference implementation, so I'd prefer confirmation from the BIP authors before proceeding.\r\n\r\nAlso, I corrected the PR description: padding the selectors changes 60 TXFS_CONTROL hashes; the remaining 90 txhash values are unchanged.",
